# Git blame — ignore these commits when computing line-level blame.
# Bulk format / rename passes belong here: including them hides the actual
# author of every line they touched.
#
# Format: one 40-char (or abbreviated) SHA per line, with the commit
# subject as a comment above it. Configure git once with:
#
#     git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# Deliberately empty — there are no bulk-reformat commits to ignore yet.
#
# Note that `git blame --ignore-revs-file` FAILS on an unknown rev rather
# than skipping it, so a stale or mistyped SHA here breaks blame for
# everyone who has the config set. Add entries only for commits that
# exist on the default branch.
